  "story": "Andrew's second tree. Any route that ends in an exit now ends in a hiring gamble: the new hire leaves in year one 30% of the time (a second search: GBP 10k recruiting + GBP 7.5k lost productivity), and whoever sits in the seat inherits the job's own drag 'e' (GBP 4k a year, here a range from 0 to 8k). With e = 4k the expected cost of the replacement L = 0.3 x 17.5k + 3 x 4k = 17,250, so an exit costs 47,250 and the coaching threshold falls from 43% to 13k / 47.25k = 27.5%.",
